 of Aquitaine]] had held this as one of their minor titles, so it had passed to Eleanor from her father; giving it to her son was effectively a revival of the title, separating it from the dukedom. Some authorities say he also held the title of &quot;Archbishop of York&quot;, but this is probably an error. His bastard half-brother [[Geoffrey, Archbishop of York|Geoffrey Plantagenet]] (d. 1212), who was born within months of William, did later hold that office, causing the confusion.

