      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Baffinisland.png|thumb|right|Baffin Island, Nunavut.]]
'''Baffin Island''' ([[Inuktitut]]: ''Qikiqtaaluk'' &amp;#5503;&amp;#5229;&amp;#5509;&amp;#5206;&amp;#5335;&amp;#5251;, French: ''île de Baffin'') is one of the [[Arctic Islands (Canada)|Arctic Islands]] in the north of [[Canada]] and is part of the territory of [[Nunavut]]. It is the largest island in Canada and is the [[List of islands by size|5th largest island in the world]], with an area of 507&amp;nbsp;451&amp;nbsp;km² (195,928 sq mi). It has a population of 11,000 ([[2004]]). It is named for [[Great Britain|British]] explorer [[William Baffin]] and was known to the [[Norseman|Norse]] as [[Helluland]].

==Geography==

[[Iqaluit]], formerly [[Frobisher Bay]], the capital of Nunavut, is located on the southern coast, on the geographical feature for which it was named until 1987.

To the south lies [[Hudson Strait]] and [[Quebec]] on the mainland. To the east are [[Davis Strait]] and [[Baffin Bay]] and beyond them is [[Greenland]]. On the West and North, [[Foxe Basin]], the [[Gulf of Boothia]] and [[Lancaster Sound]] separate Baffin Island from the rest of the [[archipelago]].

==Politics==
Baffin is part of the [[Qikiqtaaluk Region, Nunavut|Qikiqtaaluk Region]]. [[Image:Baffin_Island.png|thumb|right|Lambert azimuthal projection map of Baffin Island]]

'''Largest Communities''' (2001 population) 
#[[Iqaluit, Nunavut|Iqaluit]] (5,236)
#[[Pangnirtung, Nunavut|Pangnirtung]] (1,243)
#[[Pond Inlet, Nunavut|Pond Inlet]] (1,220) 
#[[Clyde River, Nunavut|Clyde River]] (785)
#[[Arctic Bay, Nunavut|Arctic Bay]] (646)
#[[Kimmirut, Nunavut|Kimmirut]] (433)

Additionally, the communities of [[Qikiqtarjuaq, Nunavut|Qikiqtarjuaq]] and [[Cape Dorset, Nunavut|Cape Dorset]] are located on offshore islands.

==Animals==
The [[Arctic hare]] is an animal that Baffin Island is famous for, as well as the [[Beluga]], a white whale that surfaces around Eardley Bay. Not much other wildlife can be found.

==Climate==
Most of Baffin Island lies above the [[Arctic Circle]] and all the communities from Pangnirtung north are subject to [[Polar night]] and the [[Midnight sun]]. For example, the eastern community of [[Clyde River, Nunavut|Clyde River]] experiences continuous sunlight from May 14th to July 28th, a period of 2½ months. In addition the long period from April 26th until May 13th and from July 29th until August 16th when [[twilight]] would be the darkest part of the day means the community would have just over 3½ months of light. In the winter the sun would set November 22nd and not rise again until January 19th of the next year. However, unlike places such as [[Alert]] twilight would occur for at least 4 hours a day.

