      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Thomas II''', (ca. [[1199]]&amp;ndash;[[1259]]) was the regent of the County of Savoy when his nephew, Boniface, was fighting abroad. He was also the [[Count of Flanders]] ([[1237]]&amp;ndash;[[1244]]) and a count in [[Piedmont (Italy)|Piedmont]] ([[1244]]&amp;ndash;[[1259]]).  He was the son of [[Thomas I of Savoy]] and [[Marguerite of Geneva]].

==Family and children==
He was married two times. First, with [[Jeanne, Countess of Flanders]], who died [[1244]], Countess of [[Flanders]] and [[Hainaut]], daughter of [[Baldwin I of Constantinople]]. This marriage was childless. Second, he married [[Beatrice of Fiechi]], niece of [[Pope Innocent IV]] and had 5 children:
# [[Thomas of Piedmont]] ([[1248]]&amp;ndash;[[16 May]] [[1282]]), pretender of Count of Savoy, married in [[1274]] to Guia of [[Burgundy]], the step-daughter of [[Philip I of Savoy]] and had 5 children:
## Philip, first of the Cadet line of Savoy-Achaea, lasting from [[1285]] to [[1418]]
## Peter
## Thomas
## Amadeus
## William
# [[Amadeus V of Savoy]] ([[1249]], [[Bourget-du-Lac]]&amp;ndash;[[16 October]] [[1323]], [[Avignon]]).
# [[Louis, Baron de Vaud]] ([[1250]] &amp;ndash; after [[10 January]] [[1302]]), Baron de Vaud, married firstly Adeline of Lorraine (d. c. [[1278]]), daughter of [[Matthias II, Duke of Lorraine]], married secondly 1278 Jeanne of Montfort (d. [[1300]]), daughter of [[Philip of Montfort, Lord of Castres]], married thirdly [[May 1]], [[1301]] Isabelle d'Aulnay (d. [[October 30]], [[1341]])
# Eleonora (d. [[6 December]] [[1296]]), married [[1270]] Louis I de Beaujeu.
# Alice (d. [[1 August]] [[1277]]).

He also had at least 3 illegitimate children.

